1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,771
‎I got you, Cheon Yeo-ri.

3
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,684
‎EPISODE 8

4
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:42,745
‎I'm sorry.
‎I was in court and missed your call.

5
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:46,666
‎I sent the police to the atelier
‎once I saw your text.

6
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:47,584
‎Okay.

7
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:50,795
‎So there's another body in this building?

8
00:02:53,923 --> 00:02:55,800
‎Split up. Get to it.

9
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:58,636
‎This way.

10
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:02,557
‎In here!

11
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,161
‎How did she know there was a body here?

12
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:28,249
‎Was this how she found Jang Eun-ju's body?

13
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:35,673
‎I told you I'm Si-o,
‎so that makes me him!

14
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,842
‎Let go of me!

15
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:39,802
‎Come on.

16
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,679
‎You must've been startled.

17
00:03:58,154 --> 00:03:59,447
‎Cheon Yeo-ri, you really…

18
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:01,407
‎What is going on?

19
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:05,495
‎Should I actually
‎let off a bomb this time?

20
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,583
‎My Ha-ri filmed this herself.

21
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,878
‎Isn't it so weird and unsettling?

22
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:18,800
‎If it were anyone else, seeing ghosts

23
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:20,760
‎wouldn't be such a problem.

24
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:25,014
‎But for someone who could become
‎the chairperson of Reina Group

25
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,475
‎to be going around
‎doing such bizarre things…

26
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,103
‎Isn't that unacceptable?

27
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,438
‎The company is at a critical juncture,

28
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:35,483
‎and she's only creating
‎trouble for herself.

29
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:38,987
‎Even her failed engagement six years ago
‎sent the stock price tumbling.

30
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,239
‎Speaking of which,

31
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:46,160
‎we'd like to call an extraordinary
‎shareholders' meeting soon.

32
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:50,290
‎We were hoping that you, Director Gong,

33
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:53,376
‎along with the other elders
‎who were loyal to the late chairman,

34
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:56,296
‎would throw your support behind us.

35
00:04:56,379 --> 00:04:59,465
‎If we hold an extraordinary
‎shareholders' meeting,

36
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:00,425
‎the agenda would be…

37
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:05,471
‎A motion for the removal
‎of Reina's CEO, of course.

38
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:21,654
‎What is it you wanted to say?

39
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:24,407
‎You said you wanted to wait for Yeo-ri.

40
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:27,118
‎It's about the rumors
‎that have been going around about her.

41
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:29,871
‎I wanted us to watch this together.

42
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:44,469
‎Something similar happened
‎with Seung-jae last time.

43
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,763
‎You know Yeo-ri was photographed

44
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,556
‎where Jang Eun-ju's body was found, right?

45
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,143
‎This time, another body was found
‎where Yeo-ri had gone.

46
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,395
‎She identified exactly where it was

47
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:57,148
‎as if someone had told her
‎where to look.

48
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,610
‎I heard the deceased was Si-o.

49
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:03,071
‎Wasn't he the art director for Reina?

50
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:13,706
‎It's true that

51
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:15,792
‎Si-o is dead.

52
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:19,045
‎It's also true that his body was there.

53
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:21,339
‎Don't try to brush this off
‎as another coincidence.

54
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:25,093
‎Cha Gi-u told me the same thing, Grandma.

55
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:28,221
‎She only got away
‎because he refused to testify.

56
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:30,765
‎First, Jang Eun-ju's death
‎and now this incident.

57
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:34,143
‎When coincidences keep happening,

58
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:36,145
‎there has to be a reason, right?

59
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:44,153
‎Grandma, it's clear
‎that Yeo-ri is still haunted.

60
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:49,200
‎How can someone who lets ghosts
‎guide her to corpses run a company?

61
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,202
‎What happened?

62
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:53,412
‎The truth is…

63
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:02,672
‎Mr. Ma had asked for my help.

64
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:07,260
‎He found out that Si-o was an art director
‎who had worked with us

65
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:09,178
‎and asked if I could identify him.

66
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,848
‎Mr. Ma meant to accompany me,

67
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:15,351
‎but he got held up,
‎and I ended up arriving first.

68
00:07:16,352 --> 00:07:18,855
‎Grandma, you know
‎that doesn't make sense.

69
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:21,649
‎It's obvious she just made up that excuse.

70
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:22,650
‎Why doesn't it make sense?

71
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:24,444
‎And you.

72
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,529
‎You tailed me?

73
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:30,741
‎I know what you're trying to achieve
‎with these stunts,

74
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:34,162
‎but you can't beat me
‎with tricks like that.

75
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:39,625
‎Ha-ri.

76
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,127
‎You can leave now.

77
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:44,589
‎Grandma.

78
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,356
‎I'm disappointed in you too.

79
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:06,444
‎Whatever the reason,
‎you shouldn't give her any leverage.

80
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:09,655
‎I'm sorry.

81
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,949
‎The directors of our affiliates,
‎including Gong,

82
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:14,619
‎will make this an issue
‎like they did six years ago.

83
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:18,831
‎Here's what we'll do.

84
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:21,667
‎Mr. Ma.

85
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:25,129
‎He's had a standard elite career path,

86
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:29,050
‎and those in legal circles say
‎he's upright and incorruptible.

87
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,468
‎And his looks…

88
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:34,597
‎aren't too bad either.

89
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:38,392
‎Let's set a date
‎for the engagement ceremony.

90
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:08,422
‎Gang-uk.

91
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:12,051
‎Can we meet tomorrow?

92
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:22,270
‎You made it.

93
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:27,483
‎This is Siena Hall?
‎I like the look and atmosphere.

94
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:32,154
‎My dad gifted it to my mom
‎for their tenth wedding anniversary.

95
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,574
‎I see. It's a really special place then.

96
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:36,867
‎How did they meet?

97
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:40,830
‎My dad studied architecture.

98
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:44,542
‎He traveled to Siena, Italy
‎while studying abroad in Spain,

99
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:46,419
‎and met my mom there.

100
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:50,673
‎So he named it after where they first met?

101
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:53,217
‎Man, that's so romantic.

102
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:57,805
‎If Director Ok takes over Reina Group,

103
00:09:58,514 --> 00:10:00,433
‎the first thing she'll do
‎is tear this building down.

104
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:04,770
‎And then she'll turn what's left
‎into an art gallery.

105
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,189
‎Then I'll no longer

106
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:10,484
‎be able to protect this place.

107
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:13,988
‎We can't let that happen.
‎I'll fight for Siena too.

108
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:20,077
‎Were you able to explain
‎the video Ha-ri took that day?

109
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:26,917
‎Actually, that made things worse for us.

110
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:30,838
‎My grandma wants us to get engaged
‎as soon as possible,

111
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,716
‎before the rumors spread further.

112
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:35,885
‎What should we do?

113
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:41,307
‎It looks like we might actually have to
‎hold an engagement ceremony.

114
00:10:43,225 --> 00:10:46,479
‎That's too much to ask from you, isn't it?

115
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:54,028
‎It's not.

116
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:55,905
‎I'd actually prefer it.

117
00:10:57,531 --> 00:10:58,658
‎At first,

118
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:01,327
‎I was afraid to be around you.

119
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:03,579
‎And the ghosts too.

120
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:08,000
‎But you were shouldering
‎everything on your own

121
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:12,421
‎so you wouldn't burden me
‎or anyone around you.

122
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:15,508
‎That's not something just anyone can do.

123
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,677
‎It shows how kind

124
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:22,014
‎and how warm you are as a person.

125
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:29,939
‎I wish others could see that too.

126
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:32,942
‎Now,

127
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,986
‎when I think of you,

128
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:39,448
‎my heart softens and I feel butterflies.

129
00:11:40,157 --> 00:11:41,659
‎The sky seems clearer too.

130
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:47,832
‎Even standing here with you
‎feels like a gift to me.

131
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,876
‎So if we were to get engaged,

132
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:53,170
‎I'm all for it.

133
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,048
‎Because my feelings for you…

134
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,342
‎are genuine, Yeo-ri.

135
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:18,612
‎Because my feelings for you
‎are ‎genuine, ‎Yeo-ri.

136
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:34,879
‎-We heard from Singapore.
‎-Yes?

137
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:38,257
‎They want us to confirm attendance
‎by the end of the week.

138
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:41,010
‎Just tell them

139
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:43,762
‎we'll be attending for now.

140
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:48,893
‎Tell them we'll inform them later
‎whether it'll be me or Mr. Bong attending.

141
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:50,311
‎Yes, ma'am.

142
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:55,983
‎-You can go.
‎-Oh, right.

143
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:01,447
‎-Hello.
‎-Hey.

144
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,410
‎What happened? Did you sprain your ankle?

145
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:07,411
‎Yeah, on the stairs.

146
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:10,331
‎Hyeong-min, got any pain relief patches?

147
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:12,166
‎-I'm fine.
‎-No, I don't.

148
00:13:12,249 --> 00:13:15,211
‎Mr. Ma, you know
‎a bit about hand acupuncture.

149
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:16,337
‎-Hand acupuncture?
‎-Forget it.

150
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,464
‎I do have a license,
‎but how'd you know that?

151
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:19,965
‎I saw it in your car last time.

152
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:23,052
‎I keep one in the car just in case.

153
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:24,053
‎My grandma always worries…

154
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:26,180
‎Grandma.

155
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:30,392
‎What's going on? Is she ill?

156
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:31,435
‎No, it's not that.

157
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,687
‎The Black Monkey…

158
00:13:35,147 --> 00:13:36,982
‎Pil-dong, what should I do?

159
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:39,777
‎About what?
‎Can you at least tell me what's going on?

160
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:42,696
‎Did anyone oppose or disapprove
‎when you married your wife?

161
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,406
‎-Totally.
‎-People did disapprove

162
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:45,574
‎-because of the age gap.
‎-It's ten years.

163
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,368
‎-Hey, it's just seven.
‎-Right, seven years.

164
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:49,745
‎That means she's a year older than Yeo-ri.

165
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,790
‎-What's her zodiac sign?
‎-Her zodiac sign is a goat.

166
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:53,707
‎-A goat?
‎-Yeah.

167
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,709
‎Year of the goat, a year older.

168
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:57,628
‎-Pil-dong.
‎-Yeah?

169
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:00,714
‎Can you lend me your wife's ‎saju?
‎I swear it'll save my life.

170
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:05,052
‎I can't save you if you don't tell me
‎exactly what's going on.

171
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:05,970
‎So the thing is…

172
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,181
‎I need to get engaged soon.

173
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:12,268
‎Right, you're getting engaged… What?

174
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,811
‎You're getting engaged?

175
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:17,064
‎-Yeah.
‎-What kind of stupidity is this?

176
00:14:17,147 --> 00:14:19,858
‎-What are you thinking?
‎-Jeez.

177
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:20,943
‎Use your words.

178
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:27,074
‎What if she's someone who grew up
‎without a proper upbringing?

179
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:32,329
‎You're getting engaged,
‎and you didn't even tell me?

180
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:35,165
‎If you'd told me sooner,
‎I'd have taken a better look at her.

181
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:38,127
‎Were you trying to sneak out
‎your engagement announcement

182
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:40,337
‎like a snake slithering over a wall?

183
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:42,172
‎Huh?

184
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:47,052
‎Look, it's not like I'd call it off
‎even if you disapproved.

185
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:50,639
‎What if you asked Yeo-ri weird questions

186
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,057
‎and ended up scaring her off?

187
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:56,645
‎That's why I had her tell you
‎we were just close friends.

188
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,647
‎Jeez.

189
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:00,566
‎Come on, Grandma.

190
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:03,527
‎She's a really good person,
‎and she's pretty.

191
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,031
‎Fine then.

192
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,533
‎Okay. Go ahead.

193
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:12,703
‎As long as you like her,
‎I won't disapprove.

194
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:14,830
‎-Really?
‎-However,

195
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:16,624
‎there's something I need.

196
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,000
‎Need what?

197
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:21,795
‎What do you mean, "what?"
‎Her ‎saju,‎ of course, and her zodiac.

198
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:24,882
‎Who cares about that in this day and age?

199
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:26,675
‎I don't care about anything else.

200
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,262
‎Checking her ‎saju
‎and zodiac is the bare minimum.

201
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,597
‎That's practically everything!

202
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,643
‎Why are you so reluctant?

203
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:41,106
‎Don't tell me her zodiac sign is…

204
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,735
‎-the Black…
‎-No, nothing's black.

205
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:46,820
‎Then what?

206
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,657
‎What year was she born?

207
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,701
‎The year of the goat. She's a White Goat.

208
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:57,539
‎It's a good match.

209
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,041
‎It's very good.

210
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,210
‎-Are you sure?
‎-Yes.

211
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:04,630
‎It's the best ‎saju
‎for a civil servant's wife.

212
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:10,427
‎-Is that so?
‎-The husband is surrounded by temptation

213
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,346
‎and could suffer from many mishaps,

214
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:16,642
‎but the wife's ‎saju‎ is enough
‎to save and protect him through it all.

215
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:18,602
‎You should push for this marriage.

216
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:23,357
‎Well, Gang-uk isn't the type
‎to fall for any temptation.

217
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,025
‎But then again,

218
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:29,697
‎being a prosecutor
‎comes with its share of risks and dangers.

219
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:34,785
‎Anyway, since you say
‎they're a good match,

220
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:37,454
‎I feel at ease now.

221
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:40,165
‎-Go ahead.
‎-Really?

222
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:44,420
‎You mean she passed?

223
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:48,257
‎I'll call you back
‎as soon as the date is set.

224
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:51,218
‎Okay. I love you, Madam Pang.

225
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:52,136
‎Bye.

226
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,847
‎It's a yes. She approved.

227
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,641
‎Man, I was terrified that she'd catch on.

228
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:02,479
‎Wait, what about the one-year age gap
‎between my wife and Ms. Cheon?

229
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,606
‎My grandma has no reason to check her ID.

230
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,525
‎I'm sure she'll take my word for it.

231
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:09,445
‎How did you even think
‎to use his wife's ‎saju?

232
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:11,989
‎Madam Pang is too quick-witted
‎for her own good.

233
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:15,534
‎I knew it'd be safer to give her
‎an existing ‎saju‎ than something made up.

234
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:17,119
‎Yes, that's true.

235
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:21,206
‎Before we got married,
‎my mom asked someone about my wife's ‎saju.

236
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,291
‎-Okay.
‎-Turns out,

237
00:17:22,374 --> 00:17:27,421
‎my wife's ‎saju‎ is the perfect fit
‎for a civil servant's wife.

238
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:30,632
‎Gang-uk and I have a lot in common,

239
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:33,135
‎so I guess that's why
‎we got similar fortune-telling results.

240
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,221
‎What do you and Mr. Ma have in common?

241
00:17:36,305 --> 00:17:38,307
‎I find it very frustrating

242
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,684
‎that I even need to spell it out for you.

243
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:41,602
‎Look.

244
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:43,812
‎-We're both civil servants.
‎-Okay.

245
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,814
‎-Ma is smart and capable.
‎-That's right.

246
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:47,524
‎-I'm capable too.
‎-Sure.

247
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,359
‎Ma has good looks.

248
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:52,654
‎-Forget it. What kind of reaction is that?
‎-I didn't say anything.

249
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:55,199
‎Aside from the age gap
‎that my wife and I have,

250
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:59,244
‎I can't think of a single thing
‎Gang-uk and I don't have in common.

251
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,788
‎-You're right.
‎-Of course.

252
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,998
‎-You're extra eloquent today.
‎-It's nothing.

253
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,709
‎So are all hurdles cleared now, Mr. Ma?

254
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,877
‎No more obstacles?

255
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,378
‎That's right. None left.

256
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:09,963
‎I think?

257
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,674
‎-A formal family meeting?
‎-Yeah.

258
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:15,511
‎I can't meet my in-laws for the first time
‎at the engagement ceremony.

259
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:19,807
‎His grandmother is his only family left,
‎so we should meet her.

260
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,268
‎I'm sorry things keep snowballing
‎because of me.

261
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:24,770
‎No, don't be sorry.

262
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:27,523
‎My grandmother mentioned
‎a formal family meeting too.

263
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:31,860
‎So I'll bring her to Reina Hotel
‎next Wednesday then?

264
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:33,654
‎Yes.

265
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:34,571
‎Yeo-ri.

266
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,408
‎Since we've decided to take the plunge,
‎why don't we make the best of it?

267
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:41,036
‎"We"?

268
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:43,956
‎See you on Wednesday then.

269
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,457
‎Okay.

270
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,507
‎-The lady in the white dress?
‎-Yeah!

271
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,550
‎She was so--

272
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:56,885
‎-Hello.
‎-Hello.

273
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,434
‎You can get in.

274
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:05,686
‎-Pardon?
‎-Okay.

275
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:06,812
‎Thank you.

276
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:08,397
‎Thank you.

277
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:30,836
‎-Goodbye.
‎-Goodbye.

278
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,299
‎Take care.

279
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:41,889
‎She's not at all like the rumors.

280
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:42,806
‎Right?

281
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:46,310
‎-She's even prettier up close.
‎-Yeah, totally.

282
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:48,687
‎No way. Matching rings?

283
00:19:50,105 --> 00:19:51,315
‎It's an engagement ring.

284
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:52,900
‎He gave it to me yesterday.

285
00:19:53,483 --> 00:19:55,152
‎He asked me out to eat,

286
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:56,987
‎-then suggested we take a walk.
‎-Okay.

287
00:19:57,070 --> 00:20:00,032
‎Then he said we should sit on a bench,
‎so I did without a second thought.

288
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:03,243
‎Suddenly, he got down on one knee
‎and put the ring on my finger.

289
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,370
‎It must've been nice.

290
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,581
‎-What about you, Ms. Eom?
‎-Me?

291
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,458
‎"What's this?"

292
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:10,375
‎It was in my ice cream.

293
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,462
‎I almost swallowed my own engagement ring.

294
00:20:13,545 --> 00:20:14,713
‎Why didn't you?

295
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:15,631
‎I should have.

296
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,719
‎Oh, let's see.

297
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,472
‎Hey.

298
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,390
‎I should've picked you up, Grandma.

299
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:28,018
‎I'm sorry.
‎I had to wrap up a case urgently.

300
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:30,145
‎Goodness, don't apologize.

301
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:32,147
‎Your work should always come first.

302
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:36,318
‎I arrived safe and sound,
‎so take your time.

303
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,528
‎What? You're already there?

304
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:40,113
‎Okay. I'll hurry over.

305
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,240
‎You do that.

306
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:49,831
‎So this is where
‎my granddaughter-in-law works.

307
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,501
‎As you instructed,

308
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:55,712
‎we decorated the dining room
‎so it looks simple yet classy.

309
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,965
‎I also gave the kitchen
‎special instructions

310
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,217
‎to cater the meal to the elderly.

311
00:21:01,885 --> 00:21:04,179
‎Goodness, I forgot my medication.

312
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,640
‎I'll go get it
‎and bring it to the dining room.

313
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:14,815
‎Oh, dear.

314
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:17,359
‎Are you feeling unwell?

315
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:18,735
‎No, I'm fine.

316
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:21,738
‎You could end up falling over
‎and hurting yourself.

317
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,323
‎Lean on me.

318
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:25,033
‎Let's go sit down over there.

319
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:26,243
‎Come along.

320
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:27,661
‎Oh, my.

321
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:30,414
‎Your bones must be heavier than they look.

322
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,834
‎Hello?

323
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:36,378
‎Oh, really?

324
00:21:36,461 --> 00:21:38,297
‎I'll come downstairs then. Thank you.

325
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,805
‎You look terribly pale.

326
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:49,683
‎Should I call the paramedics for you?

327
00:21:49,766 --> 00:21:51,727
‎No. I just need to rest for a while.

328
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:52,644
‎Thank you.

329
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:58,608
‎MY GANG-UK

330
00:22:02,070 --> 00:22:02,904
‎Hey.

331
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:05,032
‎Yeah.

332
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:09,328
‎I'm right inside the entrance,
‎on the couches.

333
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:11,496
‎Oh, you're bringing your girlfriend?

334
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:14,082
‎Okay. That's fine.

335
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,834
‎I'll sit right here and wait.

336
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:16,752
‎Okay.

337
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:17,794
‎Bye.

338
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:25,093
‎I'm waiting here to meet
‎my grandson's wife-to-be.

339
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:27,429
‎What brings you here?

340
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:29,222
‎I'm here on similar business.

341
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,724
‎To meet your grandson's girlfriend?

342
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:33,477
‎No, my granddaughter's boyfriend.

343
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:37,355
‎Goodness, what a coincidence this is.

344
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:43,111
‎My grandson's girlfriend works here.

345
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,615
‎Really? In which department?

346
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:48,283
‎I don't know anything about that.

347
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:50,535
‎I do know that she's lovely.

348
00:22:51,369 --> 00:22:54,289
‎According to her ‎saju,
‎she'll make a perfectly devoted housewife

349
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:56,666
‎to support and assist
‎her civil servant husband.

350
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:58,502
‎So I'm welcoming her with open arms.

351
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:01,171
‎What about you?

352
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,590
‎Do you like
‎your granddaughter's boyfriend?

353
00:23:04,299 --> 00:23:05,509
‎Well, yes.

354
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:06,468
‎Yes?

355
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:12,182
‎I'm relieved since he seems willing
‎to support my granddaughter.

356
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:18,063
‎After all, it's not uncommon for a man
‎to move in with his wife's family now.

357
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:20,816
‎Oh, he plans to move in with your family?

358
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:26,613
‎Well, these days,
‎many women have a career.

359
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:30,659
‎You're very blessed. Congratulations.

360
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,994
‎Yes, thank you. That goes for you too.

361
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:35,330
‎Yes, it does. Thank you.

362
00:23:36,706 --> 00:23:37,958
‎-Grandma!
‎-Grandma!

363
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:51,513
‎This is my grandmother, ma'am.

364
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,433
‎This is my grandmother, ma'am.

365
00:23:57,811 --> 00:24:01,898
‎Perhaps we were meant to meet
‎the way we did.

366
00:24:01,982 --> 00:24:02,899
‎Perhaps so.

367
00:24:03,525 --> 00:24:06,027
‎I am quite fond of
‎my future granddaughter-in-law.

368
00:24:07,070 --> 00:24:09,114
‎I'm into fortune-telling and reading ‎saju,

369
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:11,783
‎so I had their compatibility checked.

370
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:14,578
‎I was told they're a good match

371
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:16,371
‎as their zodiac signs are a horse and--

372
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:18,790
‎-Oh, my.
‎-What's wrong?

373
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:19,833
‎You…

374
00:24:21,209 --> 00:24:22,043
‎Are you all right?

375
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,129
‎Yes. The water went down the wrong pipe.

376
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:25,088
‎I'm sorry.

377
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:27,591
‎-Are you okay?
‎-I'm fine.

378
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:30,969
‎Do you care about fortunes and ‎saju

379
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:33,805
‎and things of that nature?

380
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:34,848
‎Things like that?

381
00:24:35,765 --> 00:24:37,350
‎Oh, yes, I do.

382
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,270
‎But not this time.

383
00:24:41,104 --> 00:24:42,814
‎Their marriage has already been decided,

384
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:44,649
‎and I didn't want to jinx anything.

385
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,359
‎They're not children either,

386
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,862
‎so I decided to respect their decision.

387
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:49,779
‎I see.

388
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:53,992
‎As I said, the fortune-teller
‎said they're a good match.

389
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:58,413
‎There's one thing that bothers me though.

390
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:01,499
‎You didn't mean
‎what you said earlier, did you?

391
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:05,962
‎About having your grandson-in-law move in.

392
00:25:06,504 --> 00:25:08,548
‎I'm not sure if you're aware,

393
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:12,594
‎but Gang-uk attended
‎the most prestigious university in Korea.

394
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,387
‎After he was admitted,

395
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:18,725
‎he passed the bar exam
‎before he even graduated.

396
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:21,269
‎What was it called?
‎Coming first in a state exam!

397
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:23,647
‎No, let's say
‎he passed with flying colors.

398
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:27,317
‎He was known to have a brilliant mind
‎and passed the bar with flying colors.

399
00:25:27,859 --> 00:25:31,780
‎So to have him move in with your family…

400
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:36,326
‎-There's no way I'd accept or allow that.
‎-Be quiet, Grandma.

401
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:37,786
‎You be quiet.

402
00:25:38,453 --> 00:25:40,956
‎-That's what I think.
‎-I see.

403
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:44,793
‎You mentioned
‎a devoted housewife earlier, right?

404
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:48,505
‎-Well…
‎-We no longer live in such an era.

405
00:25:48,588 --> 00:25:51,925
‎I'm not sure how to explain this.

406
00:25:52,008 --> 00:25:53,051
‎Although Yeo-ri

407
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:56,429
‎had to withdraw halfway through
‎due to personal reasons,

408
00:25:56,513 --> 00:25:59,349
‎she attended the top school in the US,

409
00:25:59,432 --> 00:26:01,142
‎Wharton School,
‎to get a global MBA degree.

410
00:26:01,768 --> 00:26:05,272
‎She was smart enough
‎to secure a spot there easily.

411
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:07,148
‎-She currently manages this hotel,
‎-What's she talking about?

412
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:08,942
‎-It ranks even higher.
‎-but in the future,

413
00:26:09,025 --> 00:26:14,281
‎she will likely take over
‎and manage Reina Group as a whole.

414
00:26:14,364 --> 00:26:16,866
‎So she desperately needs a husband
‎who can support her.

415
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:19,494
‎Oh, please. A husband supporting his wife?

416
00:26:19,577 --> 00:26:22,038
‎It's not like Gang-uk
‎is an incapable fool.

417
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:26,042
‎He's a very busy man.
‎He can't assist your granddaughter.

418
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:27,544
‎Is that what you think?

419
00:26:28,503 --> 00:26:30,338
‎No, of course I should
‎assist and support Yeo-ri.

420
00:26:32,215 --> 00:26:33,466
‎I should.

421
00:26:36,136 --> 00:26:38,221
‎I also support Gang-uk myself, ma'am.

422
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:40,849
‎You saw it that day, didn't you?

423
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:42,392
‎I'll get the gate right away.

424
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:48,231
‎If it's to help Gang-uk,

425
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:50,859
‎I can go anywhere and do anything.

426
00:26:50,942 --> 00:26:53,486
‎Isn't that how a wife shows real support?

427
00:26:56,281 --> 00:26:59,242
‎Something is a bit off here.

428
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,244
‎Did you have to talk such nonsense?

429
00:27:01,328 --> 00:27:05,165
‎I had to because she talked about
‎having you move in with her family.

430
00:27:05,248 --> 00:27:08,126
‎I won't let you move in with your in-laws
‎and get stomped all over.

431
00:27:08,209 --> 00:27:11,338
‎Still, you can't say you'll reconsider
‎when it's already been decided.

432
00:27:13,673 --> 00:27:16,426
‎Why did you lie to me?

433
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:20,388
‎She owns a number of motels…
‎I mean, hotels.

434
00:27:20,472 --> 00:27:21,473
‎She's a rich heiress.

435
00:27:21,556 --> 00:27:24,893
‎I didn't lie to you.
‎I just didn't tell you everything.

436
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:27,729
‎And why does it matter
‎how many hotels Yeo-ri owns?

437
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:30,607
‎I made my decision based on her alone.
‎Don't you trust me?

438
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:35,445
‎You should marry an ordinary girl
‎from an ordinary family.

439
00:27:35,528 --> 00:27:39,616
‎Other than the fact that she's pretty,
‎she's completely ordinary.

440
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:41,368
‎She doesn't brag about being rich.

441
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:42,786
‎And let's be honest,

442
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:45,205
‎you said you only cared
‎about her zodiac sign.

443
00:27:45,288 --> 00:27:47,749
‎It's not fair to pull the plug now.

444
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:48,750
‎That's right.

445
00:27:48,833 --> 00:27:53,421
‎Come to think of it, Shaman Sim
‎got your fortunes completely wrong.

446
00:27:53,922 --> 00:27:56,633
‎-I should call to yell at him for--
‎-No, Grandma.

447
00:27:57,675 --> 00:28:00,095
‎I want you to like Yeo-ri.

448
00:28:00,178 --> 00:28:02,222
‎That would make me really happy.

449
00:28:03,306 --> 00:28:04,432
‎Please?

450
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:06,518
‎Why you little…

451
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:08,978
‎-Do you like her that much?
‎-Yes, so much.

452
00:28:09,562 --> 00:28:10,647
‎Oh, dear.

453
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:13,817
‎Oh, goodness.

454
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:17,654
‎Fine.

455
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:21,408
‎Don't forget that I have your back.

456
00:28:21,491 --> 00:28:23,368
‎Don't you ever let them intimidate you.

457
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:25,787
‎-Got it?
‎-You bet.

458
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:28,206
‎I'm your grandson after all. Right?

459
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:31,042
‎It's all over for good now.

460
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:32,335
‎Let's drink. Cheers!

461
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:35,839
‎Did the zodiac thing work?

462
00:28:37,715 --> 00:28:41,428
‎They forgot all about that
‎when they started bragging about us.

463
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,389
‎This is why you shouldn't do bad things.

464
00:28:44,472 --> 00:28:45,765
‎Karma comes back around.

465
00:28:46,349 --> 00:28:49,102
‎What if she finds out?
‎Don't you need a plan or something?

466
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:50,270
‎Whatever.

467
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:52,772
‎I'll only worry about
‎what's happening right now.

468
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:53,815
‎That's right, Mr. Ma.

469
00:28:54,482 --> 00:28:55,692
‎You can worry about that later.

470
00:28:56,985 --> 00:28:58,945
‎Pil-dong, people really disapproved
‎of your marriage, right?

471
00:28:59,028 --> 00:29:00,572
‎-Yeah, a bit.
‎-Right?

472
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:01,990
‎I bet it was really bad.

473
00:29:02,073 --> 00:29:05,076
‎I wouldn't call it "really bad."
‎Like I said, the age gap was…

474
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:09,080
‎But you know, people recognize it
‎when a couple is meant to be together.

475
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:11,416
‎If someone is good enough,
‎they eventually see it.

476
00:29:11,499 --> 00:29:16,796
‎I'm putting up a wall to keep you safe.

477
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,965
‎Every now and then,

478
00:29:19,048 --> 00:29:23,636
‎I want to drink
‎among some ordinary people.

479
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,931
‎Seriously, your wife is so beautiful.

480
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:28,725
‎Why do you hate going home after work?

481
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:32,896
‎It boils down to their personality
‎and temperament.

482
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:38,026
‎Hello?

483
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:40,236
‎Have you eaten yet, Yeo-ri?

484
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:42,447
‎No, not yet.

485
00:29:43,573 --> 00:29:44,783
‎What about you?

486
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:45,950
‎Oh, I'm…

487
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:48,203
‎You're having dinner.

488
00:29:49,496 --> 00:29:52,040
‎With Investigator Ko and Hyeong-min?

489
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:53,082
‎Yes.

490
00:29:54,542 --> 00:29:58,254
‎Yeo-ri, I think we've done
‎almost everything together,

491
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:01,841
‎but we haven't eaten
‎together much, have we?

492
00:30:02,717 --> 00:30:04,177
‎-We haven't?
‎-No.

493
00:30:05,553 --> 00:30:08,056
‎Hyeong-min recommended
‎some popular eateries.

494
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:09,182
‎He insisted I take you.

495
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:11,851
‎Are you free tomorrow?

496
00:30:11,935 --> 00:30:12,852
‎I am.

497
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:20,985
‎So where is this popular eatery?

498
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:22,195
‎What?

499
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:24,239
‎Oh, it's…

500
00:30:25,907 --> 00:30:28,618
‎I'll get the details from Hyeong-min
‎and send you the link.

501
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:30,995
‎And actually…

502
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:34,040
‎There's something I must do with you
‎before we get engaged.

503
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:35,834
‎What's that?

504
00:30:36,501 --> 00:30:38,253
‎You'll find out when we meet tomorrow.

505
00:30:39,629 --> 00:30:42,048
‎Okay then. See you tomorrow.

506
00:30:42,131 --> 00:30:43,174
‎Bye.

507
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:48,596
‎Hey, Hyeong-min.

508
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,764
‎Hyeong-min.

509
00:30:50,306 --> 00:30:53,601
‎-Give me a list of the popular hangouts.
‎-Popular hangouts?

510
00:30:53,685 --> 00:30:56,062
‎-Are we going for a second round?
‎-Cut it out and hurry.

511
00:30:57,689 --> 00:31:02,485
‎Something he needs to do with me
‎before we get engaged?

512
00:31:06,155 --> 00:31:07,115
‎What?

513
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:09,993
‎Proposing with a ring?

514
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:11,870
‎No way.

515
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:17,667
‎The ceremony is coming up.

516
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:20,628
‎I guess

517
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:23,756
‎I do need a ring.

518
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:53,202
‎Man, this doesn't look right.

519
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:30,823
‎Yeo-ri.

520
00:32:46,089 --> 00:32:49,509
‎This is where the soccer player,
‎Cha Hyeon-u, proposed to his wife.

521
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:52,804
‎I see.

522
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:56,474
‎-Here are your desserts.
‎-Thank you.

523
00:32:58,059 --> 00:32:59,227
‎It's an engagement ring.

524
00:32:59,727 --> 00:33:00,561
‎It was in my ice cream.

525
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,730
‎I almost swallowed my own engagement ring.

526
00:33:24,711 --> 00:33:28,089
‎Apparently, he hid the ring
‎in the ice cream.

527
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:30,967
‎Do people still propose like that?

528
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:41,477
‎Are you all right?

529
00:33:41,561 --> 00:33:42,520
‎Yes.

530
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:47,817
‎After we're done, shall we go for a walk?

531
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:49,193
‎It's really nice out.

532
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:51,612
‎-Go for a walk?
‎-Yeah.

533
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:53,406
‎He asked me out to eat,

534
00:33:53,489 --> 00:33:54,657
‎then suggested we take a walk.

535
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:00,413
‎The flowers are in full bloom.

536
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:01,873
‎They are.

537
00:34:02,498 --> 00:34:03,332
‎How pretty.

538
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:09,005
‎Then he said we should sit on a bench,
‎so I did without a second thought.

539
00:34:09,088 --> 00:34:11,424
‎Suddenly, he got down on one knee
‎and put the ring on my finger.

540
00:34:12,633 --> 00:34:13,676
‎Just a moment, Yeo-ri.

541
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:16,095
‎Wait, right here and now?

542
00:34:21,601 --> 00:34:23,644
‎I got something on my shoe.

543
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:26,564
‎On your shoe?

544
00:34:28,316 --> 00:34:29,525
‎There, all done.

545
00:34:30,109 --> 00:34:31,152
‎Your shoe, huh?

546
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:37,700
‎Your feet must hurt.

547
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:39,577
‎No, it's fine.

548
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:43,498
‎Shall we sit down for a bit?

549
00:34:44,999 --> 00:34:45,875
‎Sure.

550
00:34:49,378 --> 00:34:50,463
‎-Here?
‎-Yes.

551
00:34:51,839 --> 00:34:53,174
‎Hold on, Yeo-ri.

552
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:57,178
‎Cover up with this.

553
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,013
‎Thank you.

554
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:06,938
‎You won't sit with me?

555
00:35:10,733 --> 00:35:11,943
‎What's wrong?

556
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:14,987
‎You might find this a bit uncomfortable,

557
00:35:16,405 --> 00:35:19,700
‎but I need to give you something
‎before we get engaged.

558
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:23,996
‎Like what?

559
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,748
‎Stay right here and rest for a bit.

560
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:27,542
‎I left it in the car. I won't be long.

561
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:29,127
‎-Wait here.
‎-Well…

562
00:35:29,210 --> 00:35:30,711
‎Take your time.

563
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,562
‎Gosh, why do you keep
‎getting down on your knee?

564
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,317
‎Yeo-ri.

565
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,471
‎My hand acupuncture needle?

566
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:06,807
‎How come…

567
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:09,018
‎Wait a minute. Why is this…

568
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:11,103
‎-Why--
‎-I'm leaving.

569
00:37:12,146 --> 00:37:13,814
‎Just a minute. Wait…

570
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:20,279
‎Wait. Stop, Yeo-ri!

571
00:37:20,363 --> 00:37:22,531
‎Yeo-ri, wait. Yeo-ri!

572
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:24,242
‎Exactly.

573
00:37:25,159 --> 00:37:27,954
‎It just happened to be in a box

574
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:30,081
‎that looked exactly like a ring box.

575
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:33,251
‎It was so embarrassing.

576
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:39,340
‎I wouldn't say I was disappointed.

577
00:37:39,423 --> 00:37:42,093
‎You know, it was just embarrassing

578
00:37:43,010 --> 00:37:44,387
‎for expecting something.

579
00:37:46,430 --> 00:37:48,349
‎The engagement ceremony's coming up,

580
00:37:49,225 --> 00:37:51,185
‎and I guess I'd gotten my hopes up.

581
00:37:57,817 --> 00:37:59,860
‎Is that from a set of matching rings?

582
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:05,449
‎I see.

583
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:07,994
‎That's what it's like.

584
00:38:09,704 --> 00:38:10,997
‎How did I mess that up?

585
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:18,004
‎-"Gang-uk."
‎-Stay still.

586
00:38:20,214 --> 00:38:21,215
‎"You want to marry me?"

587
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:23,759
‎Hyeong-min, come here
‎and hold his hand still.

588
00:38:23,843 --> 00:38:25,970
‎Are you not allowed to touch her hand?

589
00:38:26,053 --> 00:38:29,890
‎There's a reason for this, okay?
‎Just stay still this time.

590
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:31,767
‎-Keep still.
‎-You're so gruff.

591
00:38:31,851 --> 00:38:32,977
‎Come on, cooperate.

592
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:35,980
‎We're almost there.

593
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:42,528
‎Man, I even practiced
‎until I had it perfect.

594
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:47,158
‎Seriously…

595
00:38:54,206 --> 00:38:57,626
‎Hello, this is Gang-uk's grandmother.

596
00:38:57,710 --> 00:38:58,711
‎Yes, hello.

597
00:38:59,295 --> 00:39:00,880
‎I hope everything is fine on your end.

598
00:39:00,963 --> 00:39:02,965
‎Yes, thanks to you.

599
00:39:04,091 --> 00:39:05,676
‎It's just that

600
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:09,430
‎there's some news about Gang-uk.

601
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:11,390
‎Did something happen to Mr. Ma?

602
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:14,685
‎Oh, it's not bad news.
‎It's good news, actually.

603
00:39:16,479 --> 00:39:20,649
‎He's met a nice young lady
‎and hopes to get married soon.

604
00:39:21,442 --> 00:39:23,652
‎They'll hold an engagement ceremony first,

605
00:39:23,736 --> 00:39:27,073
‎and the wedding will happen
‎when the time is right.

606
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:29,992
‎That's great news. Congratulations.

607
00:39:30,618 --> 00:39:32,036
‎Thank you.

608
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:37,333
‎I owe this all to you
‎and your son, Ji-hwan…

609
00:39:39,794 --> 00:39:43,506
‎I'm so grateful
‎and sorry for everything.

610
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,597
‎Not at all.

611
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:53,349
‎I'm so happy for you.

612
00:39:55,601 --> 00:39:57,603
‎So what's the young lady like?

613
00:39:58,771 --> 00:39:59,939
‎Oh, well,

614
00:40:00,022 --> 00:40:01,315
‎in some sense,

615
00:40:02,108 --> 00:40:06,278
‎she's too good for him
‎that I can't help but be concerned.

616
00:40:07,321 --> 00:40:08,364
‎But what can I say

617
00:40:08,989 --> 00:40:11,784
‎when Gang-uk insists he's in love?

618
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:13,911
‎Yes, of course.

619
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:16,163
‎If he likes her, that's all that matters.

620
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:17,206
‎If you're free,

621
00:40:17,957 --> 00:40:20,918
‎would you like to come?

622
00:40:23,754 --> 00:40:26,757
‎I'm actually in New York right now,

623
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:28,300
‎so I have other plans.

624
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:31,137
‎I see. That won't work out then.

625
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:33,347
‎I hope your plans go well.

626
00:40:34,557 --> 00:40:37,184
‎Feel free to call me whenever you wish.

627
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:40,229
‎I will. Congratulations again.

628
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:42,690
‎Thank you. Goodbye now.

629
00:40:52,741 --> 00:40:54,702
‎The donor's heart has been removed.

630
00:40:58,706 --> 00:40:59,540
‎Grandma?

631
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:40,247
‎The engagement ceremony date is set.

632
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:44,376
‎I thought it'd be better
‎to tell you myself

633
00:41:45,294 --> 00:41:47,254
‎than to have you hear it
‎from someone else.

634
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:53,093
‎I appreciate that,

635
00:41:55,596 --> 00:41:56,764
‎but I can't say I'm happy for you.

636
00:41:58,599 --> 00:42:00,559
‎I was actually confident until now.

637
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:04,688
‎But for the first time, I have regrets.

638
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:07,149
‎I should've come back to Korea sooner.

639
00:42:10,361 --> 00:42:12,029
‎Love is all about timing, after all.

640
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:14,323
‎I guess I missed out…

641
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,327
‎on the first time.

642
00:42:20,621 --> 00:42:21,956
‎"The first time"?

643
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:25,626
‎You knew I liked you, didn't you?

644
00:42:29,171 --> 00:42:30,548
‎It hurts a lot, actually.

645
00:42:33,342 --> 00:42:34,176
‎But Yeo-ri.

646
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:37,012
‎I'm not giving up.

647
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:41,934
‎I'll just have to do things differently
‎from now on.

648
00:42:45,187 --> 00:42:46,230
‎I should go.

649
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:54,196
‎Min-hwan.

650
00:42:57,032 --> 00:42:58,367
‎You came to see Yeo-ri.

651
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,579
‎You must've heard
‎about the engagement then.

652
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:05,249
‎Come on.

653
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:08,460
‎You sounded so confident last time,
‎I thought you had a plan.

654
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:10,462
‎I'll be in touch.

655
00:43:22,808 --> 00:43:24,560
‎-Ma!
‎-Hey.

656
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:26,854
‎Do you have lunch plans today?

657
00:43:26,937 --> 00:43:28,314
‎Not exactly.

658
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:31,191
‎Good. How about we have lunch together?

659
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:33,235
‎There are people I'd like you to meet.

660
00:43:34,236 --> 00:43:35,654
‎-Sure.
‎-Great.

661
00:43:35,738 --> 00:43:37,406
‎Here.

662
00:43:38,032 --> 00:43:41,827
‎Ma, this group isn't for just anyone.

663
00:43:41,910 --> 00:43:45,789
‎We let you in without a screening
‎because you'll marry into the Reina Group.

664
00:43:46,665 --> 00:43:49,960
‎People love to gossip,
‎saying we just married up.

665
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:52,212
‎But let's be honest, they're just jealous.

666
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:54,131
‎Oh, of course.

667
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:57,384
‎By the way,
‎thanks for your help last time.

668
00:43:58,052 --> 00:43:58,969
‎Not at all.

669
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:00,346
‎What's this about?

670
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:03,265
‎My brother-in-law
‎was found guilty of bribery,

671
00:44:03,349 --> 00:44:05,476
‎but he processed his resignation
‎without further penalties.

672
00:44:05,559 --> 00:44:08,187
‎Thanks to you,
‎I saved face with my in-laws.

673
00:44:08,270 --> 00:44:10,439
‎Good. That's great to hear.

674
00:44:11,273 --> 00:44:14,234
‎Park, I'm the one who got
‎that troublemaker brother-in-law

675
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:16,779
‎an executive job at my wife's company.

676
00:44:16,862 --> 00:44:19,239
‎Of course I'm grateful for that.

677
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,450
‎But I managed to get the case dropped

678
00:44:21,533 --> 00:44:25,287
‎when a subsidiary of your wife's company
‎was charged with breaking the labor laws.

679
00:44:27,122 --> 00:44:28,874
‎-Cheers.
‎-Let's drink.

680
00:44:28,957 --> 00:44:30,125
‎All right.

681
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:34,129
‎By the way, Ma.

682
00:44:34,213 --> 00:44:37,341
‎Remember that we let you in
‎without a screening, all right?

683
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:39,718
‎I'm talking about Reina.

684
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:41,720
‎They're famous for their golf courses.

685
00:44:41,804 --> 00:44:43,806
‎We get to book free rounds
‎whenever we want, right?

686
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:49,269
‎Free rounds, my ass.

687
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,148
‎If you want to play golf,
‎pay for it out of your own pockets.

688
00:44:53,232 --> 00:44:54,650
‎As for what I heard today,

689
00:44:54,733 --> 00:44:57,569
‎I'll be reporting them directly
‎to the inspector general's office.

690
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:01,448
‎Man, how I wish I could unhear that.

691
00:45:03,992 --> 00:45:05,160
‎That just ruined my day.

692
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:17,214
‎He's much more of a jerk than I'd heard.

693
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:20,509
‎I did some digging,
‎but there wasn't much dirt.

694
00:45:21,301 --> 00:45:24,430
‎And there's too little time
‎to set him up for a trap.

695
00:45:25,597 --> 00:45:29,393
‎The best we can do for now
‎is have him demoted to a regional office.

696
00:45:29,476 --> 00:45:30,769
‎How does that sound?

697
00:45:30,853 --> 00:45:32,646
‎I don't think that would hurt him enough.

698
00:45:33,355 --> 00:45:34,648
‎Thanks anyway.

699
00:45:34,731 --> 00:45:36,191
‎I'll arrange a dinner soon.

700
00:45:36,275 --> 00:45:37,359
‎All right. See you soon.

701
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:43,699
‎CIVIL SERVANT PERSONNEL FILE

702
00:45:55,502 --> 00:45:56,670
‎Hello, sir.

703
00:45:58,213 --> 00:46:00,382
‎No need to thank me.
‎You're our primary bank.

704
00:46:01,675 --> 00:46:03,469
‎I'd like to pay you a visit soon.

705
00:46:05,179 --> 00:46:06,180
‎Yes, but…

706
00:46:07,097 --> 00:46:09,725
‎I'd like someone else to join us that day.

707
00:46:10,309 --> 00:46:11,560
‎That must be him.

708
00:46:15,272 --> 00:46:16,523
‎Hello, Vice President.

709
00:46:16,607 --> 00:46:18,609
‎Director Gong, what perfect timing.

710
00:46:19,318 --> 00:46:20,652
‎What do you mean by that?

711
00:46:20,736 --> 00:46:24,156
‎You know the CEO of CL Group,
‎Kang Min-hwan, right?

712
00:46:25,741 --> 00:46:28,243
‎My goodness, it's been a while.

713
00:46:28,994 --> 00:46:29,828
‎What brings you here?

714
00:46:29,912 --> 00:46:32,247
‎This is the bank
‎we do most of our business with.

715
00:46:32,331 --> 00:46:33,999
‎I was hoping to see you one day.

716
00:46:34,500 --> 00:46:36,001
‎What a pleasant surprise.

717
00:46:38,003 --> 00:46:40,088
‎How did you figure out
‎I'd taken out a loan

718
00:46:40,172 --> 00:46:42,341
‎from the bank on my Reina shares?

719
00:46:44,676 --> 00:46:45,886
‎That loan matures soon.

720
00:46:46,637 --> 00:46:49,014
‎You can't repay the debt in full, can you?

721
00:46:50,098 --> 00:46:53,060
‎At this rate,
‎the bank will take it all.

722
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:55,354
‎I'll think of a solution.

723
00:46:57,689 --> 00:46:58,857
‎Why would you do that?

724
00:47:01,026 --> 00:47:03,237
‎Is CL Group interested in Reina Group?

725
00:47:03,737 --> 00:47:05,197
‎If that's not the case,

726
00:47:05,280 --> 00:47:07,991
‎is this something personal
‎that involves CEO Cheon Yeo-ri?

727
00:47:08,992 --> 00:47:12,454
‎I was surprised to hear
‎who she'd chosen to marry.

728
00:47:12,538 --> 00:47:15,541
‎Everyone who's in the know
‎in this industry

729
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:18,210
‎knows you have feelings for her.

730
00:47:18,293 --> 00:47:20,379
‎Given the current circumstances,

731
00:47:20,879 --> 00:47:24,758
‎I figured she'd choose you
‎even if it were for strategic reasons.

732
00:47:25,300 --> 00:47:27,678
‎I can always create new circumstances.

733
00:47:28,428 --> 00:47:29,846
‎When that time comes,

734
00:47:30,889 --> 00:47:32,599
‎the stake you hold could be of great help.

735
00:47:42,859 --> 00:47:46,405
‎CHAIRWOMAN BAEK GYEONG-JA

736
00:47:48,532 --> 00:47:50,534
‎A share transfer was reported to the FSS.

737
00:47:51,451 --> 00:47:53,245
‎Was it on Director Ok's end? How much?

738
00:47:53,328 --> 00:47:55,038
‎Enough to pose a threat.

739
00:47:55,872 --> 00:47:57,749
‎If they get any more
‎than they already have,

740
00:47:57,833 --> 00:48:00,919
‎the affiliate directors' share
‎could become the deciding vote.

741
00:48:04,089 --> 00:48:05,132
‎What's the matter, ma'am?

742
00:48:06,967 --> 00:48:08,635
‎Call Yeo-ri.

743
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:09,928
‎Will do, ma'am.

744
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:19,479
‎Grandma.

745
00:48:22,274 --> 00:48:23,567
‎What happened?

746
00:48:23,650 --> 00:48:25,485
‎Her condition suddenly worsened,

747
00:48:25,569 --> 00:48:27,070
‎so we had her admitted for a check-up.

748
00:48:27,696 --> 00:48:29,489
‎This is already the second time.

749
00:48:29,573 --> 00:48:33,327
‎It means I'm at an age
‎where I can't guarantee my health.

750
00:48:35,954 --> 00:48:36,955
‎Yeo-ri.

751
00:48:37,039 --> 00:48:40,834
‎Let's have the engagement ceremony
‎and then the wedding as soon as possible.

752
00:48:40,917 --> 00:48:44,463
‎That way, I can gift Mr. Ma
‎some company shares.

753
00:48:45,672 --> 00:48:46,632
‎Company shares?

754
00:48:46,715 --> 00:48:48,842
‎That has been done before, right?

755
00:48:48,925 --> 00:48:51,762
‎Yes. Most recently,
‎the chairman of PA Group

756
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:56,099
‎gifted 200,000 shares
‎to his son-in-law after the wedding.

757
00:48:56,183 --> 00:48:58,310
‎It's just so we're prepared.

758
00:48:58,393 --> 00:49:01,813
‎The FSS received a report
‎of a stock transfer.

759
00:49:02,856 --> 00:49:03,982
‎Considering the timing,

760
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:07,069
‎they could host a sudden
‎extraordinary shareholders' meeting.

761
00:49:08,111 --> 00:49:10,489
‎It's what they did six years ago.

762
00:49:11,323 --> 00:49:12,574
‎And the agenda…

763
00:49:13,241 --> 00:49:14,910
‎will be a motion for my removal.

764
00:49:31,843 --> 00:49:34,137
‎REINA HOTELS & RESORTS
‎HEIRESS CHEON YEO-RI'S ENGAGEMENT

765
00:49:34,221 --> 00:49:36,515
‎TO PROSECUTOR MA GANG-UK
‎SET TO HAPPEN PRIVATELY AT SIENA HALL

766
00:49:43,230 --> 00:49:45,524
‎12 YEARS AGO

767
00:49:45,607 --> 00:49:46,983
‎-Where are you going?
‎-Huh?

768
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:49,528
‎I told you.
‎I'm going on a trip with Yeo-ri.

769
00:49:49,611 --> 00:49:52,364
‎Your dad's flying home
‎from his business trip today.

770
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:53,281
‎Do you have to go?

771
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:56,243
‎Dad flies home once a week,

772
00:49:56,952 --> 00:49:58,704
‎but this is my first trip with Yeo-ri.

773
00:49:58,787 --> 00:50:01,498
‎Goodness, Yeo-ri is all you talk about.

774
00:50:01,581 --> 00:50:03,291
‎Does she know you're like this?

775
00:50:03,375 --> 00:50:06,128
‎Not yet. I might tell her on this trip.

776
00:50:06,628 --> 00:50:09,131
‎Sons are a lost cause once they grow up.

777
00:50:09,214 --> 00:50:11,091
‎I'll be going. And watch your fingers.

778
00:50:11,883 --> 00:50:14,094
‎Wait, Ji-hwan. Come here.

779
00:50:14,177 --> 00:50:15,011
‎What is it?

780
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:16,680
‎Where's your pendant?

781
00:50:17,264 --> 00:50:18,306
‎-My pendant?
‎-Yeah.

782
00:50:23,603 --> 00:50:24,688
‎It's right here.

783
00:50:25,939 --> 00:50:28,859
‎What if it falls out of your pocket?

784
00:50:28,942 --> 00:50:31,570
‎I told you to wear it at all times.
‎Turn around.

785
00:50:31,653 --> 00:50:33,405
‎I don't like wearing
‎accessories like this.

786
00:50:35,574 --> 00:50:40,036
‎You know you can't go anywhere
‎without this, don't you?

787
00:50:40,537 --> 00:50:41,955
‎It's your grandmother's orders.

788
00:50:42,038 --> 00:50:44,791
‎She hates it when you make plans
‎to go somewhere.

789
00:50:46,209 --> 00:50:47,127
‎Mom.

790
00:50:49,087 --> 00:50:51,047
‎You know this is ridiculous, right?

791
00:50:51,131 --> 00:50:52,674
‎How can a single pendant

792
00:50:52,758 --> 00:50:54,718
‎keep ghosts away from someone?

793
00:50:54,801 --> 00:50:58,180
‎There are things
‎that even science can't explain.

794
00:50:59,431 --> 00:51:03,727
‎Your grandmother feels better
‎knowing you're wearing this,

795
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:05,812
‎so be a good grandson and keep it on.

796
00:51:05,896 --> 00:51:08,815
‎For her sake
‎and her prayers for you, okay?

797
00:51:09,357 --> 00:51:11,443
‎But why just me when we're twins?

798
00:51:11,526 --> 00:51:13,361
‎She doesn't make Min-hwan wear this.

799
00:51:13,945 --> 00:51:15,197
‎Am I fated to die young?

800
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:18,825
‎-How could you say such a thing, Ji-hwan?
‎-That hurt.

801
00:51:18,909 --> 00:51:20,994
‎It's just that she makes
‎such a fuss over me.

802
00:51:21,077 --> 00:51:22,329
‎Ji-hwan.

803
00:51:22,412 --> 00:51:24,122
‎Min-hwan. Let's go.

804
00:51:24,748 --> 00:51:27,876
‎I'll take good care of Ji-hwan.
‎Don't you worry.

805
00:51:28,585 --> 00:51:30,003
‎Okay. Have fun.

806
00:51:30,086 --> 00:51:31,963
‎-See you.
‎-Let's go.

807
00:51:32,464 --> 00:51:33,632
‎Don't worry too much.

808
00:51:39,721 --> 00:51:40,931
‎Bye, Mom.

809
00:51:45,852 --> 00:51:49,022
‎You really think wearing that
‎will keep ghosts away?

810
00:51:52,192 --> 00:51:54,027
‎You have to live. I'll die instead.

811
00:52:04,704 --> 00:52:05,789
‎Yeo-ri!

812
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:30,063
‎Min-hwan!

813
00:52:32,148 --> 00:52:33,066
‎Min-hwan!

814
00:52:34,234 --> 00:52:35,193
‎Kang Min-hwan.

815
00:53:08,768 --> 00:53:11,813
‎-Swap out any soggy ones, okay?
‎-Got it, sir.

816
00:53:11,897 --> 00:53:13,440
‎These can't be eaten if they're soggy.

817
00:53:13,523 --> 00:53:14,649
‎Understood.

818
00:53:14,733 --> 00:53:17,402
‎-Top up the wine a bit more.
‎-Yes, sir.

819
00:53:17,485 --> 00:53:19,029
‎Be sure to check for allergies.

820
00:53:19,112 --> 00:53:22,157
‎She has a large farm,
‎and she supplied the strawberries.

821
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:23,408
‎Please, have a taste.

822
00:53:26,202 --> 00:53:29,122
‎The person is unavailable.
‎You will be redirected to--

823
00:53:38,256 --> 00:53:42,344
‎PLEASE JOIN US FOR THE ENGAGEMENT PARTY
‎OF CHEON YEO-RI AND MA GANG-UK

824
00:54:03,782 --> 00:54:05,367
‎GANG-UK

825
00:54:07,285 --> 00:54:08,370
‎Gang-uk?

826
00:54:08,453 --> 00:54:12,248
‎Sorry, I couldn't answer your call
‎because I kept getting calls from work.

827
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:14,918
‎Where are you now?

828
00:54:15,001 --> 00:54:17,587
‎I'm heading toward the elevator
‎at the basement parking lot.

829
00:54:18,713 --> 00:54:20,465
‎So you're at the hotel, right?

830
00:54:20,548 --> 00:54:22,801
‎Yes. I just got into the elevator.

831
00:54:24,135 --> 00:54:25,136
‎I'll be up soon.

832
00:54:25,804 --> 00:54:26,846
‎Yeo-ri, are you…

833
00:54:29,015 --> 00:54:31,267
‎CALL ENDED

834
00:54:39,359 --> 00:54:41,319
‎What? What's happening?

835
00:54:43,697 --> 00:54:46,741
‎The person is unavailable.
‎You will be redirected to voicemail--

836
00:54:56,710 --> 00:54:57,836
‎Min-hwan.

837
00:54:57,919 --> 00:54:59,087
‎I came to say something.

838
00:54:59,963 --> 00:55:00,797
‎Right now?

839
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:04,009
‎Can it wait? I have to go somewhere.

840
00:55:04,092 --> 00:55:05,510
‎I need to tell you now.

841
00:55:07,887 --> 00:55:08,847
‎Six years ago,

842
00:55:10,015 --> 00:55:11,725
‎I came to Korea as soon as
‎I heard about your engagement.

843
00:55:14,602 --> 00:55:16,771
‎I wanted to do whatever I could
‎to change your mind.

844
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:18,398
‎Don't come closer.

845
00:55:19,357 --> 00:55:21,276
‎-Gi-u.
‎-Stay right there!

846
00:55:22,318 --> 00:55:23,903
‎I didn't think I'd actually become haunted

847
00:55:24,863 --> 00:55:26,322
‎just by holding your hand.

848
00:55:29,659 --> 00:55:30,660
‎I'm sorry.

849
00:55:31,244 --> 00:55:33,288
‎I don't think I can marry you. I'm sorry.

850
00:55:42,922 --> 00:55:43,757
‎But…

851
00:55:45,175 --> 00:55:47,552
‎I couldn't approach you,
‎even seeing how distraught you were.

852
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:51,389
‎I was almost relieved…

853
00:55:54,017 --> 00:55:56,311
‎because I thought
‎I'd be able to stick around.

854
00:55:59,189 --> 00:56:00,398
‎But was I too late?

855
00:56:02,275 --> 00:56:03,568
‎Once again, this is what it's come to.

856
00:56:05,653 --> 00:56:06,738
‎Yeo-ri.

857
00:56:07,322 --> 00:56:09,616
‎I've liked you for a very long time.

858
00:56:12,368 --> 00:56:14,037
‎I don't want to lose you this time.

859
00:56:15,455 --> 00:56:16,414
‎Min-hwan.

860
00:56:17,582 --> 00:56:18,458
‎I'm sorry.

861
00:56:19,667 --> 00:56:20,627
‎I've never

862
00:56:21,628 --> 00:56:23,713
‎thought of you that way.

863
00:56:24,923 --> 00:56:25,799
‎Yeo-ri.

864
00:56:25,882 --> 00:56:27,509
‎I feel uncomfortable

865
00:56:28,093 --> 00:56:29,219
‎talking about this with you.

866
00:56:33,306 --> 00:56:34,474
‎Just like Cha Gi-u,

867
00:56:35,475 --> 00:56:36,851
‎what if Gang-uk can't make it either?

868
00:56:43,191 --> 00:56:44,651
‎Will you be okay with being alone again?

869
00:56:57,122 --> 00:56:59,749
‎You can hold my hand, Yeo-ri.

870
00:57:04,629 --> 00:57:05,797
‎Damn it.

871
00:57:27,902 --> 00:57:30,155
‎Excuse me?

872
00:57:30,238 --> 00:57:31,448
‎The doors won't open!

873
00:57:53,219 --> 00:57:54,637
‎Just like Cha Gi-u,

874
00:57:54,721 --> 00:57:56,222
‎what if Gang-uk can't make it either?

875
00:57:59,642 --> 00:58:02,020
‎Excuse me? The doors won't open!

876
00:58:05,023 --> 00:58:06,566
‎Stay right there!

877
00:58:07,233 --> 00:58:08,943
‎I didn't think I'd actually become haunted

878
00:58:09,027 --> 00:58:11,696
‎-just by holding your hand.
‎-What if Gang-uk can't make it either?

879
00:58:12,655 --> 00:58:13,907
‎Is anyone there?

880
00:58:17,118 --> 00:58:17,994
‎I'm sorry.

881
00:58:18,077 --> 00:58:19,954
‎I don't think I can marry you. I'm sorry.

882
00:58:20,038 --> 00:58:21,122
‎I won't date her.

883
00:58:21,206 --> 00:58:22,373
‎I won't see Yeo-ri ever again.

884
00:58:22,457 --> 00:58:23,500
‎Don't come closer.

885
00:58:24,709 --> 00:58:25,960
‎Don't come any closer!

886
00:59:07,210 --> 00:59:08,378
‎Are you all right, Yeo-ri?

887
00:59:14,551 --> 00:59:15,552
‎Gang-uk.

888
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:19,430
‎The elevator stopped all of a sudden.

889
00:59:19,514 --> 00:59:20,348
‎I'm sorry.

890
00:59:23,685 --> 00:59:25,645
‎I thought you wouldn't make it.

891
00:59:26,229 --> 00:59:29,524
‎Why wouldn't I make it
‎when I've been waiting for this day?

892
00:59:36,614 --> 00:59:37,657
‎Before we go inside…

893
00:59:38,658 --> 00:59:41,953
‎I wasn't sure what you'd like,
‎so I picked something out myself.

894
00:59:44,622 --> 00:59:45,540
‎What do you think?

895
01:00:14,694 --> 01:00:16,362
‎I was so scared.

896
01:00:19,949 --> 01:00:21,367
‎I wondered if it were the ghosts,

897
01:00:23,995 --> 01:00:26,873
‎or if I was afraid
‎of yet another failed engagement.

898
01:00:30,918 --> 01:00:32,170
‎I guess it was neither.

899
01:00:37,091 --> 01:00:39,135
‎I was just afraid you wouldn't come.

900
01:00:41,888 --> 01:00:42,889
‎That I would…

901
01:00:45,016 --> 01:00:46,684
‎never get to see you again.

902
01:00:49,270 --> 01:00:51,189
‎That's what I was afraid of.

903
01:00:54,233 --> 01:00:55,360
‎Why wouldn't you see me again?

904
01:00:56,277 --> 01:00:57,445
‎I told you

905
01:00:58,196 --> 01:01:00,365
‎that I'll be by your side,
‎wherever you are.

906
01:01:08,247 --> 01:01:09,165
‎I think

907
01:01:10,875 --> 01:01:12,377
‎I really want to…

908
01:01:14,629 --> 01:01:16,339
‎get engaged to you.

909
01:01:30,061 --> 01:01:30,937
‎Will you

910
01:01:32,438 --> 01:01:33,773
‎be my fiancé?

911
01:02:59,275 --> 01:03:01,694
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

912
01:03:02,612 --> 01:03:05,198
‎Siena Hall's at the center of attention
‎since Yeo-ri's engagement.

913
01:03:05,281 --> 01:03:08,826
‎An extraordinary shareholders' meeting
‎will be held at Reina soon.

914
01:03:08,910 --> 01:03:10,495
‎Is it a serious situation?

915
01:03:10,995 --> 01:03:13,122
‎The dismissal of Cheon Yeo-ri,
‎CEO of Reina Hotel.

916
01:03:13,206 --> 01:03:15,249
‎Ok Gye-hui knows no fear.

917
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:16,250
‎When will they start?

918
01:03:16,334 --> 01:03:17,293
‎Right away.

919
01:03:17,877 --> 01:03:20,046
‎-Do give us your full support.
‎-Gosh.

920
01:03:20,129 --> 01:03:21,798
‎Are there any shareholders
‎worth contacting?

921
01:03:21,881 --> 01:03:23,966
‎-You'll do it yourself, ma'am?
‎-I have to.

922
01:03:24,050 --> 01:03:25,760
‎Tell me what you need.
‎I'll help with anything.

923
01:03:25,843 --> 01:03:27,470
‎-No way. I won't do it.
‎-Come on.

924
01:03:28,471 --> 01:03:30,014
‎I'm going abroad on a business trip.

925
01:03:30,097 --> 01:03:32,850
‎Yeo-ri must feel cornered
‎to resort to something this ridiculous.

926
01:03:32,934 --> 01:03:35,770
‎It may seem reckless,
‎but I might try something different.

927
01:03:36,562 --> 01:03:37,563
‎Is Kang Min-hwan going too?

928
01:03:38,856 --> 01:03:41,234
‎I think I should come with you.

929
01:03:43,319 --> 01:03:48,324
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
